        <mxCell id="flow-legend" value="Flow&#10;1. SEP Lambda orchestrator enqueues async work on SQS (ktm verification queue)&#10;2. SEP Lambda submits the AWS Batch job directly (se-ktm-job-definition); Batch uses its own built-in job queue&#10;3. Batch stores task artifacts in S3 (task-scoped bucket)&#10;4. Batch reaches the student cluster over the PUBLIC EKS endpoint / ingress ALB&#10;5. dev-ingress-alb fronts the EKS development-dev cluster (183631338639)&#10;6. dev-ingress-alb also fronts the KTM shared verification cluster&#10;7. In-cluster ArgoCD reconciles the verification stack (k8s service)&#10;8. Keycloak / Gitbud run as in-cluster StatefulSets behind the cluster" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=#B3B3B3;fillColor=#FFFFFF;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="120" width="280" height="308" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend" value="Legend&#10;Solid line = primary flow&#10;Dashed line = asynchronous / event-driven flow&#10;Red = blocked / missing / disabled&#10;🆕 = new in version N&#10;🔄 = changed in version N&#10;Outer boundary = stack Boundary (captioned; provider style)&#10;Inner boundary = Network Boundary (captioned; provider style)&#10;Numbered markers (1..N) = ordered data flow steps; see Flow list&#10;AWS nodes = native-colour AWS service icons (green S3, orange Lambda, purple ALB, ...)&#10;EKS clusters are native AWS EKS; in-cluster ArgoCD/Keycloak carry their own brand marks; Gitbud named in label&#10;EKS block is a SIBLING boundary, NOT nested in the AWS VPC (foreign-leaf nesting deferred in 1.11.0)&#10;EKS reached over PUBLIC endpoint (publicAccessCidrs 0.0.0.0/0) — not peering&#10;In-cluster ArgoCD / Keycloak / Gitbud are in-cluster workloads, not separate EC2/LB resources" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=#B3B3B3;fillColor=#FFFFFF;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10" vertex="1" parent="1">
